00:33:08.810 --> 00:33:10.080
called Vision API.

00:33:10.080 --> 00:33:11.870
And what Vision API
does is exactly what

00:33:11.870 --> 00:33:14.300
I've just shown on the chart
with the neural network.

00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:16.520
One side is raw
imagery of pixels.

00:33:16.520 --> 00:33:18.830
The other right side, it
decides what those pixels

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:20.810
are based on confidence.

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:22.790
So some of the things
the models spit out

00:33:22.790 --> 00:33:25.850
is, that's a cat, that's a dog,
that's a tree, that's a car.

00:33:25.850 --> 00:33:29.360
And that's only interesting
if the model also tells you,

00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:32.450
it's a cat, and we're
99% sure it's a cat.

00:33:32.450 --> 00:33:34.429
In other words, we go
to meetings at work

00:33:34.429 --> 00:33:36.470
not because we want to
hang out with our friends,

00:33:36.470 --> 00:33:37.670
although that's
perfectly valuable.

00:33:37.670 --> 00:33:38.870
That's what bars are for.

00:33:38.870 --> 00:33:41.150
We go to meetings
so we can all agree

00:33:41.150 --> 00:33:42.950
that the data is
sufficient enough

00:33:42.950 --> 00:33:45.560
to make a decision against that
we're going to apply resources

00:33:45.560 --> 00:33:47.984
for, and thus we defer risk.

00:33:47.984 --> 00:33:49.400
So the whole idea
for a meeting is

00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:50.720
that we establish a
confidence interval

00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:52.190
that everyone finds sufficient.

00:33:52.190 --> 00:33:54.148
Typically those aren't
mathematically relevant.

00:33:54.148 --> 00:33:55.380
In this case, they are.

00:33:55.380 --> 00:33:58.090
So on the far left, I've
saved some core imagery.

00:33:58.090 --> 00:34:01.280
But each one of those images
that I ran through Vision API

00:34:01.280 --> 00:34:02.040
is one of these.

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:02.540
Let me see.

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:04.010
If I'm particularly
careful, I can

00:34:04.010 --> 00:34:07.070
scroll to where it will
actually render the image.

00:34:07.070 --> 00:34:11.540
Each one of these dots is mapped
to a logical scientific method

00:34:11.540 --> 00:34:12.570
namespace.

00:34:12.570 --> 00:34:13.880
We remember this, right?

00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:14.929
There's a null.

00:34:14.929 --> 00:34:17.030
Then it's an animal,
vegetable, mineral.

00:34:17.030 --> 00:34:20.270
If it's an animal, is it's
hot blooded, cold blooded?

00:34:20.270 --> 00:34:22.400
Is it hot blooded, cold
blooded with fur, not fur?

00:34:22.400 --> 00:34:23.441
Is it pretty, not pretty?

00:34:23.441 --> 00:34:26.150
All those sorts of things
follow along the natural tree,

00:34:26.150 --> 00:34:29.870
which is exactly how a
neural network does not work.

00:34:29.870 --> 00:34:31.719
And I'll show you
that in just a moment.

00:34:31.719 --> 00:34:32.989
So we think this way.

00:34:32.989 --> 00:34:34.739
The neural network
doesn't think this way.

00:34:34.739 --> 00:34:36.155
For those of you
that are actively

00:34:36.155 --> 00:34:38.389
working on machine learning
and using deep science,

00:34:38.389 --> 00:34:40.969
this is why your head hurts
and why most of the days

00:34:40.969 --> 00:34:42.139
fall in failure.

00:34:42.139 --> 00:34:44.870
Because you intuit why
the neural network does

00:34:44.870 --> 00:34:45.920
a particular thing.

00:34:45.920 --> 00:34:48.469
And that's OK because it doesn't
mind if you intuit or not.

00:34:48.469 --> 00:34:49.550
It does not care.

00:34:49.550 --> 00:34:50.699
It does what it does.

00:34:50.699 --> 00:34:53.239
So let me flip right
over to the number one

00:34:53.239 --> 00:34:55.860
denizen of the internet.

00:34:55.860 --> 00:34:59.600
It turns out this is
