00:45:48.250 --> 00:45:50.200
But what if you could
just compile on the fly

00:45:50.200 --> 00:45:51.706
or always be compiling?

00:45:51.706 --> 00:45:53.830
In this case, what if you
could always be training?

00:45:53.830 --> 00:45:56.680
Or, visually to you,
the fractional unit

00:45:56.680 --> 00:46:00.010
of time of training always in
the background as data changes,

00:46:00.010 --> 00:46:03.510
or as you do shifts on how
you're cleaning the data,

00:46:03.510 --> 00:46:06.730
if it's always up to speed,
you never have to take a break.

00:46:06.730 --> 00:46:08.620
You spend so much
more time iterating

00:46:08.620 --> 00:46:11.170
