algorithm choices,

00:46:11.170 --> 00:46:13.120
it moves you from a
seven month cycle,

00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:16.870
on average, for a good
model, to seven days.

00:46:16.870 --> 00:46:19.270
Seven months to seven days.

00:46:19.270 --> 00:46:20.690
And how do we do that?

00:46:20.690 --> 00:46:22.280
Let's talk about that.

00:46:22.280 --> 00:46:23.360
OK.

00:46:23.360 --> 00:46:25.000
Customers have this problem.

00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:27.740
We have this problem
when we are a customer.

00:46:27.740 --> 00:46:29.630
I need data access
in a lot of places.

00:46:29.630 --> 00:46:31.800
I need to develop,
build analytical models.

00:46:31.800 --> 00:46:33.841
A lot of these things are
kind of non-negotiable.

00:46:33.841 --> 00:46:34.970
We'll all nod our heads.

00:46:34.970 --> 00:46:37.610
These are the surface area that
we're trying to apply product

00:46:37.610 --> 00:46:39.860
to rather than just process to.

00:46:39.860 --> 00:46:42.776
Today, largely, everybody
solves these things in process

00:46:42.776 --> 00:46:44.150
if you're doing
machine learning.

00:46:44.150 --> 00:46:45.830
We'd like this to be
productized so you

00:46:45.830 --> 00:46:48.650
spend all your time doing
other, more interesting things.

00:46:48.650 --> 00:46:51.770
Because, again, 75% of
the machine learner's time

00:46:51.770 --> 00:46:53.210
is spent playing with data.

00:46:53.210 --> 00:46:55.286
None of that time
is time they want.

00:46:55.286 --> 00:46:57.410
And for many people, that's
because they're already

00:46:57.410 --> 00:46:58.520
on BigQuery.

00:46:58.520 --> 00:47:00.860
For the people that aren't
using a big data system which

00:47:00.860 --> 00:47:02.693
is a fully managed
service, they spend a lot

00:47:02.693 --> 00:47:04.250
of their time
provisioning servers,

00:47:04.250 --> 00:47:08.630
misrouting networking,
misconfiguring CPU choices,

00:47:08.630 --> 00:47:10.910
not understanding the fact
that they lose those boxes

00:47:10.910 --> 00:47:13.285
at the end of the week because
those virtual machines get

00:47:13.285 --> 00:47:14.480
reprovisioned by their CTO.

00:47:14.480 --> 00:47:16.563
You get the idea that
having these things fungibly

00:47:16.563 --> 00:47:19.340
available is actually part of
the magic for how we don't have

00:47:19.340 --> 00:47:20.990
to say there's features here.

